# byte-size Series Standard + SEO Franchise

**Owner:** Growth (SEO + content turf) · **Created 2026-06-26** · Engagement owns the vendor relationship and produces the raw vendor read; Growth turns it into a ranking, repeatable series. Proven by the Grafana Alloy byte-size (an evergreen winner). This makes "byte-size" a destination people search for and return to, not a one-off. UK English, no em dashes, §5-clean, defensible numbers only, independent + disclosed.

---

## 1. Series definition
**Naming.** Post title `byte-size: What Is <X>?`. SEO meta title `What Is <X>? A Practical Observability Guide` (the proven pattern). Slug `what-is-<x>`. Tag: `byte_size` (underscore; one canonical taxonomy).

**Structure (the proven shape, ~3 min read):**
1. **Hook intro** (2-4 lines): why this matters, the honest framing.
2. **What is it?** plain-English definition, what it does, who is behind it.
3. **[Optional] Foundational concept** when the tool rests on one (e.g., "First, what is eBPF?"). This doubles as a secondary keyword target, see §3.
4. **What it does well** (2-4 concrete strengths).
5. **The honest ledger** (the real gaps and limits). This is the brand value.
6. **Is it right for you?** a clear "who it fits / who it does not" call.
7. **CTA + disclosure + Sources.**

**Tone.** Conviction-light, plain English, vendor-neutral. UK English, no em dashes, §5-clean (run `s5_lint.py`).

**Disclosure rule (vendor pieces, mandatory).** Any byte-size on a vendor the brand has spoken with or may collaborate with carries a one-line disclosure near the close: relationship stated, opinion independent, gaps kept in. No pricing, no named customers, no unverified claims (codex §11). A Sources / further-reading block of external, verifiable links is mandatory.

**CTA.** One intent-routed CTA per the CTA library: byte-size is informational / top-of-funnel, so **Block B (newsletter)** is the routed CTA, plus the free-chapter soft secondary. (Keep the author's reply / "book a slot" line as the human close; Block B is the standard ask.)

**Diagrams (mandatory, from 2026-07-16 — Al's call).** Every byte-size carries **at least TWO diagrams** on the light in-body surface: technical / principle diagrams that explain the mechanism (a business-flow diagram is optional and additional). Held to the full diagram QA gate (two self passes + fresh-eyes independent validation, same bar as thumbnails). A picture says a thousand words, and byte-sizes exist to make a concept land, so they lean on diagrams. This supersedes the earlier ">=1 diagram" rule (GR-2026-07-15-02).

**Pull-quotes: byte-sizes are EXEMPT.** The pull-quote rule (verbatim Block Q lines: 2 per Conviction blog, 1 per newsletter) does NOT apply to byte-sizes. Byte-sizes are diagram-heavy by design, and the diagrams do the visual-anchor and comprehension job that pull-quotes do on prose blogs. See `23_PULL_QUOTE_STANDARD_PROPOSAL_2026-07-16.md` (approved 2026-07-16).

---

## 2. SEO / cluster strategy
- **Series hub + tag.** Every byte-size carries the `byte_size` tag, which gives a beehiiv tag archive (the de facto hub). Propose a curated "byte-size" hub entry in site nav + a short intro at the top of the tag archive so it reads as a series, not a tag. (Structural, filed for Control.)
- **Internal-link rule (every byte-size):** link to 2 sibling byte-size posts + the most relevant deep guide (e.g., the OpenTelemetry Collector guide), and add a reciprocal link back from at least one sibling once live. This is what compounds the cluster.
- **Cluster home:** byte-size sits in cluster C4 (Observability practice & tooling) of the Step 6 map (`11_FORWARD_SEO_STEP6.md`); definitional pieces (eBPF, OpenTelemetry, distributed tracing) can also support C2/C5.
- **Pattern, not vendor:** target the generic query ("what is X"), never "X vs Y" hit-pieces; the neutral, definitional angle is what ranks and what keeps the byline honest.
- **Tech Tuesday shares this franchise (ID-2026-07-05-02, settled in `16_TECH_TUESDAY_SEO_POSITIONING.md`):** a Tech Tuesday explainer's WRITTEN companion IS a byte-size on this contract (+ a `tech_tuesday` tag); the video is the second front door on YouTube/Spotify. One topic = one crawlable byte-size page + one video, never two competing MO URLs. Tech Tuesday gets a video hub (playlist/feed), not a separate search hub.

