## 4. Cadence + where briefs live
- **Cadence:** 1-2 byte-size per month, slotted into the existing blog pipeline (does not displace the weekly Signal Drop or the monthly Digest). Each new byte-size is rounded up in the next Observability Digest "On the blog this month".
- **Email distribution (Al, 2026-06-26): held to web-only for now.** Byte-size publishes web-only + Digest roundup until the Technical & Practitioner / Leadership & Strategy streams are populated (the survey has not run). Then byte-size becomes the email content for the **Technical stream** specifically, rather than a blast to the whole list. Holding now is sequencing, not a permanent web-only.
- **Discovery while email is held:** every byte-size ships with a social amplification pack (X + company LinkedIn + light personal LinkedIn), handed to Daily Ops for Buffer, so people learn it exists. Disclosed vendor pieces lead with the neutral angle, never a pitch.
- **Folder standard (per `04_Newsletter_and_Blog`):** each piece in its own per-post folder `04_Newsletter_and_Blog/YYYY-MM-DD_<topic>/`; briefs in `_Briefs`. (Odigos is in `2026-06-24_odigos-bite-size/`.)
- **Tech Tuesday byte-size (DO-2026-07-09-01):** a Tech Tuesday topic's WRITTEN byte-size / blog web post lives in `04_Newsletter_and_Blog/` as a normal per-post folder (`YYYY-MM-DD_<topic>/`), exactly like every other byte-size, while the Tech Tuesday franchise folder `03_Podcast/Tech_Tuesday/TT##_<slug>/` holds only the franchise assets (title card, thumbnail, intro/outro, metadata) plus a cross-link to that `04` post. The `04` post is the crawlable search anchor the episode + socials point at; the TT folder points at it, it does not duplicate the written post.
- **Hand-off:** Engagement drafts the vendor read into the per-post folder; Growth runs the SEO pass (this standard), publishes via the Bite-size template, and wires the cluster links.

